# UI theme — follow existing design

## Default

Always match the **existing SplitEase UI theme** (icon-derived indigo/amber brand, light + dark Material 3 schemes, `Se*` components, `SplitEaseColors` / `Color.kt`, Material 3 typography).

Do **not** invent alternate looks (custom accent schemes, one-off dialog skins) unless the user **explicitly** asks for a different theme or visual direction.

## Concrete rules

- Prefer `presentation/ui/Se*` building blocks (`SeScreen`, `SeModal`, `SePrimaryButton`, `SeTextButton`, `SeListRow`, etc.) over raw Material widgets with custom colors.
- New modals/dialogs → use `SeModal` / `SeModalTitle` / `SeModalBody`.
- Colors → brand vals in `presentation/theme/Color.kt`, `MaterialTheme.colorScheme` via `SplitEaseTheme`, and `SplitEaseColors` aliases. Do not hardcode hex outside theme files.
- Screenshots or third-party UI mocks are **content/layout references** only; restyle them to the app theme unless the user says otherwise.

## Exception

Only deviate when the user clearly requests a different theme, palette, or a pixel-matched custom look.
